  N = 1001 \quad \text{Check if it's a perfect square}
  $$

$$
\sqrt{1001} \approx 31.64 \quad \text{not an integer}
$$

Check next candidate perfect square divisible by 11:

$$
11 \times 92 = 1012
$$

$$
\sqrt{1012} \approx 31.81 \quad \text{not integer}
